      "id": "clothing",
      "title": "Baby Clothing & Accessories",
      "sub": "Clothing by size (NB / 0–3 / 3–6), sleep, feeding, soothing, bath, on the go",
      "guide": null,
      "info": [
        {
          "id": "buying-rules",
          "title": "Buying rules (apply to both lists)",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "ol",
              "items": [
                "**Skin-contact fabric:** GOTS-certified organic cotton first; merino wool second; cotton muslin for blankets and swaddles. GOTS is the verification — \"organic\" on a tag alone isn't.",
                "**Treat these with caution:** polyester fleece and microfiber against skin (sheds microfibers, traps heat), bamboo \"viscose/rayon\" (chemically regenerated; soft, but not the natural fiber the marketing implies).",
                "**Sleepwear:** US rules require kids' sleepwear to be either flame-resistant or snug-fitting. Choose **snug-fit cotton** (tag reads \"wear snug-fitting, not flame resistant\") — that's the untreated route.",
                "**Fragrance-free everything** — detergent, wipes, balms. No essential oils on baby in the early months.",
                "**Heat is the design constraint.** Baby is 0–3 months in May–Aug and 3–6 months in Aug–Nov. Short sleeves carry the load; a few long-sleeve pieces cover AC.",
                "**Size up bottoms for cloth diapers.** Cloth adds bulk in the seat. Bodysuits and pants run tight a size early; bodysuit extenders are a cheap fix.",
                "**Buy thin on Newborn size.** Average birth weight is ~7.5 lb; NB fits roughly 5–8 lb and many babies outgrow it in 2–4 weeks or skip it. Bulk up on 0–3. Hold most 3–6 purchases until after the shower and the first growth check — gifts pile up in exactly these sizes.",
                "**Quantities assume laundry every 2–3 days** (cloth diapers set that rhythm) and 2–4 outfit changes a day for spit-up and blowouts."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Priority key: **Must** = have before birth · **Nice** = useful, not required · **Later** = buy when the stage arrives · **Skip** = commonly sold, not needed"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
